scenario b13_fx over household_b
  tally 2
  from 2025-07-01
  note "B-13 (a) · Had the floren been 5 % cheaper (questions.md): from 2025-07-01 every floren rate, the CBL's published mid rates (fx_mid, GEN-4) and Bank Lazur's own rates (lazur_buy, B-D23 §4) alike, is the real one times 0.95, rounded to 4 decimal places, half up, as both publish theirs. Everything else as it was."
  note "Each rate is a row of this layer computed from the base's own row for the same day (L 6.4, a scenario row as an expression over the base's facts), one row per day the reality holds a rate for from 2025-07-01: the judged text's days and those of b13_rows.tally. A day the reality holds no rate for stays a hole in both worlds."
  note "The version is known 2025-06-30, the day before the change: a stipulation, as if known then (L 6.4); a replace known the same day as the row it replaces is refused by the reference interpreter (fault F5, scenarios/crash.tally of household A)."

input b13_factor: num question "By what factor is every floren rate from 2025-07-01 multiplied (questions.md B-13)?"

input b13_step: num DUK/FLR question "To what step is a scaled floren rate rounded (questions.md B-13)?"

version b13_rates
  cite questions
  governs 2025-07-01..
  known 2025-06-30
  note "questions.md B-13: each rate dated from 2025-07-01 is the real one times 0.95, rounded to 4 decimal places, half up"
  replace fx_mid = round(household_b.fx_mid * b13_factor, b13_step, half-up) governs 2025-07-01 "questions.md B-13: the CBL mid rate of 2025-07-01 (b13_rows) times 0.95, to 4 places, half up"
